% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 5 "Negation as Failure", section 5.3
%         ("Party example with negation as failure and its defeat").
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% Book: "mary will go if john will go. john will go if bob will not go."
% Here "bob will not go" is negation as failure. With no facts about bob, john
% (and hence mary, who follows john) will go; asserting "bob will go" defeats
% john's reason, so john and mary both drop out, leaving only bob. This
% demonstrates non-monotonicity: adding a fact removes conclusions.
%
% Reconstruction (matching party_looping.le): to keep the rules generic (LE
% flags rules built from bare constants), the dependencies are lifted into
% generic rules over a "follows" relation and an "is reluctant unless ... goes"
% relation, with the concrete actors supplied as scenario facts:
%   - "mary will go if john will go"     ->  mary follows john
%   - "john will go if bob will not go"  ->  john stays home only if bob,
%       the person john watches, will go (negation as failure on bob).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a person* will go.
*a first person* follows *a second person*.
*a first person* watches *a second person*.

the knowledge base party_naf includes:

% A person will go if someone they follow will go.
a first person will go
    if the first person follows a second person
    and the second person will go.

% A person who is waiting on someone they watch will go unless that
% watched person will go (negation as failure: absence of the watched
% person's attendance licenses going).
a first person will go
    if the first person watches a second person
    and it is not the case that
        the second person will go.

scenario no_bob is:
    mary follows john.
    john watches bob.
    who_goes expects answers ["john will go", "mary will go"].

scenario bob_goes is:
    mary follows john.
    john watches bob.
    bob will go.
    who_goes expects answers ["bob will go"].

query who_goes is:
    which person will go.
